; The timing harness is not part of `dune runtest`: it takes minutes, and on a
; general-purpose machine with frequency scaling and preemption it is noisy enough that
; a spurious failure would train people to ignore it. Run it deliberately:
;
;   dune exec test/timing/timing_ct.exe
;
; It is a negative test -- it can find leakage, not prove its absence -- and it reports
; INCONCLUSIVE rather than success when its own positive control goes undetected.

(executable
 (name timing_ct)
 (libraries
  mpc
  mpc.ed25519
  mirage-crypto-rng
  mirage-crypto-rng.unix
  mtime
  mtime.clock.os
  eqaf))
